{title: 595 - Let Every Lamp Be Burning}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Gm]Let every [Cm/G]lamp be burning [Eb/Bb]bright,
[Gm]The darkest hour is nearing;
[Gm]The darkest hour of earth’s long night,
[Gm]Before the Lord’s appearing.

Refrain:
[Bb7/Ab]Then trim [Cm/G]your lamps, my brethren dear,
[Eb/Bb]Then trim [Gm]your lamps with godly fear;
[Gm]The Master's coming draweth [Eb/Bb]near,
[Bb]Let every [Fm/Ab]lamp be [Cm/G]burning.

Verse 2:
[Gm]Though thousands [Cm/G]calmly slumber [Eb/Bb]on,
[Gm]The last great message spuring,
[Gm]Wel'll rest our living faith upon
[Gm]His promise of returning.

Verse 3:
[Gm]His word [Cm/G]our lamp, His truth our [Eb/Bb]guide,
[Gm]We cannot be mistaken;
[Gm]Though dangers rise on every side,
[Gm]We shall not be forsaken.

Verse 4:
[Gm]Then let [Cm/G]good works with faith appear,
[Gm]To help the world atound us;
[Gm]Obedience bring the blessing near
[Gm]When faith has firmly [Bb]bound us.
